<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-3339] get() in explicit READ_COMMITTED transaction on OFFHEAP_TIERED cache copies data from offheap to onheap.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-3339</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;On OFFHEAP_TIERED TRANSACTIONAL cache:&lt;br/&gt;
1. Put entry.&lt;br/&gt;
2. Cache size equals 1 and iterator returns one entry.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Open PESSIMISTIC READ_COMMITED transaction.&lt;br/&gt;
4. get() that value.&lt;br/&gt;
5. Commit transaction.&lt;br/&gt;
6. Cache size now equals 2 and iterator returns two identical entries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By fast investigation was found that after put() operation value goes to offheap. After get() operation in explicit transaction the same value appears in onheap and offheap iterators. As a result user sees two the same entries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pull request with test that reproduces the bug:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/817&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/817&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
